---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/common/CodeBlock.astro';
import { Terminal, Package, Sparkles, ArrowRight, Code2, Copy, Check } from 'lucide-preact';

const mainDartCode = `import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:bloom_ui/bloom_ui.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(const MyApp());
}

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      title: 'My Bloom App',
      theme: ThemeData(
        brightness: Brightness.light,
        extensions: const [BloomTheme.light], // or BloomTheme.novaLight, vegaLight, etc.
      ),
      darkTheme: ThemeData(
        brightness: Brightness.dark,
        extensions: const [BloomTheme.dark],
      ),
      home: const HomeScreen(),
    );
  }
}`;

const bloomConfigCode = `{
  "$schema": "https://bloom.dev/schema.json",
  "style": "nova",
  "rsc": false,
  "aliases": {
    "components": "lib/bloom_ui/primitives",
    "theme": "lib/bloom_ui/theme",
    "utils": "lib/bloom_ui/utils"
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="How to install and set up Bloom UI in your Flutter application."
  currentSlug="installation"
  category="Getting Started"
  toc={[
    { id: 'cli-workflow', title: 'Option 1: CLI Workflow (Recommended)' },
    { id: 'pub-package', title: 'Option 2: Pub.dev Package' },
    { id: 'setup-theme', title: 'Setup Theme & Extensions' },
    { id: 'bloom-config', title: 'Configuration File' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="space-y-4 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Installation
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Get started with Bloom UI in less than 2 minutes. Choose between the shadcn-style CLI workflow (where you own the component code) or the standard pub.dev package.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Option 1: CLI Workflow -->
    <section id="cli-workflow" class="space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-purple-500/10 text-purple-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold">
          1
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Option 1: CLI Workflow (Recommended)
        </h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The Bloom CLI manages design tokens, installs individual primitives directly into your <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">lib/bloom_ui/</code> folder, and ensures zero runtime dependencies.
      </p>

      <!-- Step 1: Install CLI -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Activate the Bloom CLI globally:</h3>
        <div class="relative rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 flex items-center justify-between">
          <code>dart pub global activate bloom_cli</code>
          <button
            onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('dart pub global activate bloom_cli'); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('bloom:toast', { detail: { title: 'Copied', message: 'Ready to paste in terminal.', type: 'emerald' } }))"
            class="p-1.5 text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition flex items-center gap-1"
            title="Copy command"
          >
            <Copy className="w-4 h-4" />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2: Init Project -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Initialize Bloom UI in your Flutter project:</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Run this command in the root of your Flutter project. It will prompt you for your preferred style theme (Nova, Vega, Maia, etc.) and write the base token system to <code class="text-purple-400">lib/bloom_ui/theme/</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="relative rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 flex items-center justify-between">
          <code>bloom ui init</code>
          <button
            onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('bloom ui init'); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('bloom:toast', { detail: { title: 'Copied', message: 'Ready to paste in terminal.', type: 'emerald' } }))"
            class="p-1.5 text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition flex items-center gap-1"
            title="Copy command"
          >
            <Copy className="w-4 h-4" />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3: Add Components -->
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Add components as needed:</h3>
        <div class="relative rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <code># Add individual components</code>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <code>bloom ui add button card dialog chart</code>
            <button
              onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('bloom ui add button card dialog chart'); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('bloom:toast', { detail: { title: 'Copied', message: 'Ready to paste in terminal.', type: 'emerald' } }))"
              class="p-1.5 text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition flex items-center gap-1"
              title="Copy command"
            >
              <Copy className="w-4 h-4" />
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-800/80 flex items-center justify-between">
            <code># Or add all 60+ components at once</code>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <code>bloom ui add all</code>
            <button
              onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('bloom ui add all'); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('bloom:toast', { detail: { title: 'Copied', message: 'Ready to paste in terminal.', type: 'emerald' } }))"
              class="p-1.5 text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition flex items-center gap-1"
              title="Copy command"
            >
              <Copy className="w-4 h-4" />
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Option 2: Pub.dev Package -->
    <section id="pub-package" class="space-y-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-pink-500/10 text-pink-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold">
          2
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Option 2: Pub.dev Package
        </h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        If you prefer managing Bloom UI as a standard pub.dev package:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="relative rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-pink-300 flex items-center justify-between">
          <code>flutter pub add bloom_ui</code>
          <button
            onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('flutter pub add bloom_ui'); window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('bloom:toast', { detail: { title: 'Copied', message: 'Ready to paste in terminal.', type: 'emerald' } }))"
            class="p-1.5 text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition flex items-center gap-1"
            title="Copy command"
          >
            <Copy className="w-4 h-4" />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Setup Theme -->
    <section id="setup-theme" class="space-y-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        Setup Theme & Extensions
      </h2>

      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Wrap your root <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">MaterialApp</code> with the <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">BloomTheme</code> extension in your <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">lib/main.dart</code>:
      </p>

      <CodeBlock code={mainDartCode} lang="dart" filename="lib/main.dart" />
    </section>

    <!-- Configuration File -->
    <section id="bloom-config" class="space-y-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        bloom.config.json
      </h2>

      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The <code class="font-mono text-purple-400">bloom.config.json</code> file at the root of your project defines your target directory, style preset, and custom aliases:
      </p>

      <CodeBlock code={bloomConfigCode} lang="json" filename="bloom.config.json" />
    </section>

    <!-- Next Page Footer -->
    <div class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex justify-between">
      <a
        href="/docs/introduction"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold text-xs hover:bg-slate-200 dark:hover:bg-slate-800 transition"
      >
        <span>Previous: Introduction</span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/docs/theming"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 rounded-2xl bg-purple-600 text-white font-bold text-xs hover:bg-purple-500 transition shadow-lg"
      >
        <span>Next: Theming & Tokens</span>
        <ArrowRight className="w-4 h-4" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
